+/// Maximum number of cells in the dense grid a `worksheet_range()` call will build, and the
+/// largest `Vec::reserve()` request the `Dimensions` record is allowed to trigger. The
+/// `Dimensions` record's declared row/column span is attacker-controlled (its extended, 14-byte
+/// form encodes the end row as a raw `u32` and end column as a raw `u16`, with no validation) -
+/// bounding both the reservation and the eventual dense-grid build avoids requesting an
+/// arbitrarily large allocation from either. Matches the cap `ods.rs`/`xlsx::mod.rs` use for the
+/// same reason.
+pub const MAX_DENSE_RANGE_CELLS: usize = 100_000_000;
